#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Discover how quantum and high-performance computing can be combined in a single workflow."
msgstr "Découvre comment le calcul quantique et le calcul haute performance peuvent être combinés dans un seul workflow."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Vue d'ensemble"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Vue d'ensemble {#overview}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![\"Hero image\"](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/index/hero.avif)\n"
msgstr "![\"Hero image\"](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/index/hero.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This course provides an overview of classical and quantum resources as well hybrid workflows with examples.\n"
msgstr "Ce cours donne un aperçu des ressources classiques et quantiques, ainsi que des flux de travail hybrides illustrés par des exemples.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recommended background {#recommended-background}"
msgstr "Prérequis recommandés {#recommended-background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This course is intended for two distinct groups of individuals: those with backgrounds in quantum computing but not in HPC, and those with backgrounds in HPC but not quantum computing. These technologies complement each other, and those with expertise in one are increasingly aware of the importance of the other. Learners can skip over sections in their own area of expertise as appropriate.\n"
msgstr "Ce cours s'adresse à deux groupes distincts : celles et ceux qui ont une formation en informatique quantique mais pas en calcul haute performance (HPC), et celles et ceux qui ont une formation en HPC mais pas en informatique quantique. Ces technologies se complètent mutuellement, et les personnes expertes dans l'une d'elles prennent de plus en plus conscience de l'importance de l'autre. Les apprenants peuvent sauter les sections relevant de leur propre domaine d'expertise, selon ce qui leur convient.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We recommend that learners complete the following prerequisite prior to this course:\n"
msgstr "Nous recommandons aux apprenants de suivre le prérequis suivant avant ce cours :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up your local environment by following along with the [Get started](/guides/) guide in our documentation page.\n"
msgstr "Configure ton environnement local en suivant le guide [Premiers pas](/guides/) dans notre documentation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a deeper understanding of quantum information, complete this optional course:\n"
"- [Basics of quantum information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information) with John Watrous.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour approfondir ta compréhension de l'information quantique, suis ce cours optionnel :\n"
"- [Les bases de l'information quantique](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information) avec John Watrous.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exam {#exam}"
msgstr "Examen {#exam}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To earn your badge for Integrating Quantum and High-Performance Computing, take the exam at IBM&reg; Training. This exam is intended to be taken after reading the lessons in this course. After you pass the exam, you will be notified by Credly that you have earned a badge.\n"
msgstr "Pour obtenir ton badge « Intégration du quantique et du calcul haute performance », passe l'examen sur IBM&reg; Training. Cet examen est destiné à être passé après avoir lu les leçons de ce cours. Après avoir réussi l'examen, tu seras notifié·e par Credly que tu as obtenu un badge.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Exam](/learning/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/exam)\n"
msgstr "[Examen](/learning/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/exam)\n"

